IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rra-remedies`

-- Retirement and Re-employment Act 1993, ss 4(3), 8, 8A, 8B, 8C, 9, 9A, 9B, 9C, 10 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_retirement-and-re-employment-act-1993_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `ss 8(1), 8A -- where and by when`

#ASSERT `Where do I take my complaint first` `I was dismissed on the ground of age before my specified age` EQUALS `written representations to the Minister to be reinstated`
#ASSERT `Where do I take my complaint first` `I was denied re-employment because no suitable vacancy was found` EQUALS `written notice to the Commissioner, then representations to the Minister to be re-employed`
#ASSERT `Where do I take my complaint first` `the employment assistance payment offered to me is unreasonable` EQUALS `a mediation request to the Commissioner, then a claim in the Employment Claims Tribunal`

#ASSERT `How many months do I have for the first step` `I was dismissed without just cause or excuse on or after my specified age` EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `How many months do I have for the first step` `the terms of my re-employment offer are unreasonable` EQUALS 6

#ASSERT `From when are those months counted` `I was denied re-employment as not meeting the eligibility criteria` EQUALS `the last day of my employment`

#ASSERT `Am I in time for the first step` `the terms of my re-employment offer are unreasonable` 6
#ASSERT NOT `Am I in time for the first step` `I was denied re-employment as not meeting the eligibility criteria` 2

#ASSERT NOT `Am I in time to make representations to the Minister after conciliation` 2

§ `ss 8(1), 8A(2), 8B(1) -- which remedy is open`

#ASSERT `Is the age-dismissal remedy in section 8 open to me` 64 65 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is the age-dismissal remedy in section 8 open to me` 65 65 TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `Is the just-cause remedy in section 8B open to me` 2011 TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the just-cause remedy in section 8B open to me` 2012 TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 8(3), 8(6), 8(8), 8B(6), 8B(12), 8B(14)`

#ASSERT `What may the Minister direct my employer to do for me` `representations under section 8` TRUE EQUALS `reinstatement with the salary I would have earned, or just and equitable compensation`
#ASSERT `What may the Minister direct my employer to do for me` `representations under section 8B` FALSE EQUALS `no direction, unless the Minister is satisfied`

#ASSERT NOT `May I still sue my employer for damages over it` TRUE

#ASSERT `Can the court recover the unpaid amount for me as if it were a fine` TRUE TRUE

§ `ss 8B(3), 8B(4), 8C(2)`

#ASSERT `Is the route I now want closed to me` TRUE `representations to the Minister under section 8B` `a Tribunal claim over the amount of the employment assistance payment`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the route I now want closed to me` FALSE `representations to the Minister under section 8B` `a Tribunal claim over the amount of the employment assistance payment`

§ `ss 4(3), 8B(13), 9A(2), 9C, 10`

#ASSERT `What is the maximum fine` `my employer dismissing me on the ground of age before my prescribed minimum retirement age` FALSE EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `What is the maximum fine` `my employer failing to comply with the Minister's direction under section 8B` FALSE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `What is the maximum fine` `my neglecting to attend as a summons requires` TRUE EQUALS 10000

#ASSERT `What is the maximum imprisonment, in months` `my neglecting to attend as a summons requires` FALSE EQUALS 6

#ASSERT `What is the most a composition can cost, if the offence is compoundable` `my obstructing or making a false statement to an investigating officer` FALSE EQUALS 1000

